messages:  [["Please act as a math teacher and solve the product problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of <<number1 such as 27>> and <<number2 such as 153>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. <<number2 153 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.>>\n1. <<Multiply number1 27 by the ones place digit 3 of number2 153>>\n2. <<Multiply number1 27 by the tens place digit 50 of number2 153>>\n<<other digits of number2 if it has>>\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: <<sum of the results>>.\nSo, the final computed product is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 596 and 932?\n# Reasoning:", "<think>\n.\nTo find the product of 596 and 932, I'll start by breaking down the multiplication into manageable parts.\n\nFirst, I'll multiply 596 by the units digit of 932, which is 2. This gives me 1,192.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 596 by the tens digit of 932, which is 30. Multiplying 596 by 30 results in 17,880.\n\nFinally, I'll multiply 596 by the hundreds digit of 932, which is 900. This multiplication yields 536,400.\n\nAfter obtaining these three partial products, I'll add them together: 1,192 + 17,880 + 536,400</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
