messages:  [["Please act as a math teacher and solve the product problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of <<number1 such as 27>> and <<number2 such as 153>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. <<number2 153 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.>>\n1. <<Multiply number1 27 by the ones place digit 3 of number2 153>>\n2. <<Multiply number1 27 by the tens place digit 50 of number2 153>>\n<<other digits of number2 if it has>>\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: <<sum of the results>>.\nSo, the final computed product is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 255 and 573?\n# Reasoning:", "<think>\n.\nTo find the product of 255 and 573, I'll start by breaking down the multiplication into manageable parts.\n\nFirst, I'll multiply 255 by the ones place of 573, which is 3. This gives me 765.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 255 by the tens place of 573, which is 70. Multiplying 255 by 70 results in 17,850.\n\nFinally, I'll multiply 255 by the hundreds place of 573, which is 500. This multiplication yields 127,500.\n\nNow, I'll add all these partial products together: 765 plus 17,850 plus 127,500</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
