      "text": "146,115.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **255** and **573**, we'll follow a step-by-step multiplication process:\n\n1. **Multiply 255 by the ones place of 573 (which is 3):**\n   \n   \\[\n   255 \\times 3 = 765\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 255 by the tens place of 573 (which is 70):**\n   \n   \\[\n   255 \\times 70 = 17,\\!850\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 255 by the hundreds place of 573 (which is 500):**\n   \n   \\[\n   255 \\times 500 = 127,\\!500\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all the partial products together:**\n   \n   \\[\n   765 + 17,\\!850 + 127,\\!500 = 146,\\!115\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{146,\\!115}\n\\]",
