      "text": "30,456.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **104** and **294**, we'll follow these steps:\n\n1. **Multiply 104 by 4 (the ones place of 294):**\n   \n   \\[\n   104 \\times 4 = 416\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 104 by 90 (the tens place of 294):**\n   \n   \\[\n   104 \\times 90 = 9,\\!360\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 104 by 200 (the hundreds place of 294):**\n   \n   \\[\n   104 \\times 200 = 20,\\!800\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all the partial products together:**\n   \n   \\[\n   416 + 9,\\!360 + 20,\\!800 = 30,\\!456\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{30,\\!456}\n\\]",
