      "text": "614,615.\n\n# Step-by-Step Solution:\n\nTo find the product of **699** and **875**, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Break down the multiplication:**\n   \n   \\[\n   699 \\times 875 = 699 \\times (800 + 70 + 5)\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 699 by each part separately:**\n\n   - **Multiply by 5:**\n     \n     \\[\n     699 \\times 5 = 3,\\!495\n     \\]\n   \n   - **Multiply by 70:**\n     \n     \\[\n     699 \\times 70 = 699 \\times 7 \\times 10 = 4,\\!893 \\times 10 = 48,\\!930\n     \\]\n   \n   - **Multiply by 800:**\n     \n     \\[\n     699 \\times 800 = 699 \\times 8 \\times 100 = 5,\\!592 \\times 100 = 559,\\!200\n     \\]\n\n3. **Add all the results together:**\n\n   \\[\n   3,\\!495 + 48,\\!930 + 559,\\!200 = 614,\\!615\n   \\]\n\n4. **Final Answer:**\n\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{614,\\!615}\n   \\]",
