messages:  [["Please act as a math teacher and solve the product problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of <<number1 such as 27>> and <<number2 such as 153>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. <<number2 153 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.>>\n1. <<Multiply number1 27 by the ones place digit 3 of number2 153>>\n2. <<Multiply number1 27 by the tens place digit 50 of number2 153>>\n<<other digits of number2 if it has>>\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: <<sum of the results>>.\nSo, the final computed product is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 447 and 539?\n# Reasoning:", "<think>\n\nTo find the product of 447 and 539, I'll start by breaking down the multiplication into smaller, more manageable parts.\n\nFirst, I'll multiply 447 by the units digit of 539, which is 9. This gives me 4,023.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 447 by the tens digit of 539, which is 30. This results in 13,410.\n\nFinally, I'll multiply 447 by the hundreds digit of 539, which is 400. This gives me 178,800.\n\nNow, I'll add all these partial products together: 4,023 + 13,410 + 178,800. This sum will give me the final product.\n</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
