messages:  [["Please act as a math teacher and solve the product problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of <<number1 such as 27>> and <<number2 such as 153>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. <<number2 153 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.>>\n1. <<Multiply number1 27 by the ones place digit 3 of number2 153>>\n2. <<Multiply number1 27 by the tens place digit 50 of number2 153>>\n<<other digits of number2 if it has>>\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: <<sum of the results>>.\nSo, the final computed product is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 191 and 339?\n# Reasoning:", "<think>\n\nTo find the product of 191 and 339, I'll start by breaking down 339 into its place values: 300, 30, and 9.\n\nFirst, I'll multiply 191 by 9, which gives me 1,719.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 191 by 30. This is the same as multiplying 191 by 3 and then adding a zero at the end, resulting in 5,730.\n\nThen, I'll multiply 191 by 300. This is equivalent to multiplying 191 by 3 and adding two zeros, which gives me 57,300.\n\nFinally, I'll add all these partial products together: 1,719 + 5,730 + 57,300. This sum will give me the final product.\n</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
