      "text": "97,745.\n\n# Step-by-Step Solution:\n\nTo find the product of **865** and **113**, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Multiply 865 by 3 (the units digit of 113):**\n   \n   \\[\n   865 \\times 3 = 2,\\!595\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 865 by 10 (the tens digit of 113, which is 1 multiplied by 10):**\n   \n   \\[\n   865 \\times 10 = 8,\\!650\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 865 by 100 (the hundreds digit of 113, which is 1 multiplied by 100):**\n   \n   \\[\n   865 \\times 100 = 86,\\!500\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all the partial products together:**\n   \n   \\[\n   2,\\!595 + 8,\\!650 + 86,\\!500 = 97,\\!745\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{97,\\!745}\n\\]",
